# Patch files are consumed by `git apply` from the PlatformIO build scripts
# (scripts/patch_sdfat.py, scripts/patch_jpegdec.py). git apply matches context
# bytes literally, so a patch that reaches the working tree with CRLF endings
# cannot apply to the LF sources it patches.
#
# core.autocrlf=true -- the common Windows default -- rewrites them on checkout,
# which fails the build for every Windows contributor with:
#
#   RuntimeError: SdFat patch does not apply: 0001-invalidate-failed-cache-fill.patch
#   error: patch failed: src/common/FsCache.cpp:39
#   error: src/common/FsCache.cpp: patch does not apply
#
# Pin the working-tree form to LF on both sides so the patch bytes and the sources
# they apply to always agree. The files themselves are already LF in the repository.
*.patch text eol=lf
